<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Card APPLINK-1 — the https pairing QR, iOS half.

	     The desktop prints `https://flowmic.app/go/pair?…` (the host is
	     PAIR_HTTPS_HOST in packages/protocol/src/constants.ts) and the phone
	     already parses it (lib/src/ui/scan_payload.dart kPairLinkPrefixHttps).
	     Until this entitlement existed, iOS had never been told this app owns
	     that domain, so scanning that QR with the system camera opened Safari
	     on a phone that HAS FlowMic. This file is the declaration; the Android
	     twin is the autoVerify intent-filter in
	     android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml.

	     THERE WAS NO ENTITLEMENTS FILE IN THIS PROJECT AT ALL before this card,
	     and no CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS build setting either — so creating the
	     file is only half the work. Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj now points
	     all three Runner configurations (Debug / Release / Profile) at it; a
	     .entitlements nobody signs with is a file, not a capability, and that
	     façade is exactly what verify/lint/applink-declarations.mjs refuses.

	     INERT UNTIL THE DOMAIN PUBLISHES ITS SIDE. iOS fetches
	     https://flowmic.app/.well-known/apple-app-site-association (through
	     Apple's CDN) and takes the link only if that file names this app's
	     Team ID + bundle id (app.flowmic.ios). That file does not exist yet —
	     publishing the hostname is the owner's decision — so today the link
	     still opens Safari. It fails closed.

	     ALSO NOT DONE, and it is not a declaration problem: nothing in the Dart
	     tree listens for an incoming pairing URL. app_links is constructed only
	     inside the login sheet (lib/src/ui/login_sheet.dart), for the
	     `flowmic://login` hand-back. So once the association file is published,
	     the OS will open FlowMic and FlowMic will do nothing with the link.
	     Routing it is a behaviour change and belongs to its own card.

	     `applinks:` only. Deliberately NOT `webcredentials:` (no password
	     autofill — this app signs in through the browser, card NR-2b) and NOT
	     `activitycontinuation:` (superseded, and there is no Handoff here). One
	     service, one reason. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:flowmic.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
